<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's MPC unit sets September IPO.</title>
<headline>Manila's MPC unit sets September IPO.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine cellular phone operator Smart Communications Co Inc plans to start its initial public offering in September, its president said on Monday.</p>
<p>The company had initially scheduled a public stock offering for the middle of the year but decided to defer it due to volatile conditions in the local and international markets.</p>
<p>&quot;September is the start of the offering period,&quot; Smart president Orlando Vea told Reuters.</p>
<p>Smart is a unit of Metro Pacific Corp. Metro's parent firm First Pacific Co Ltd and Nippon Telegraph and Telephone Corp (NTT) also have stakes in the cellular phone company.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (63 2) 841-8936, Fax 817-6267</p>
